{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the two ends of the two cords.</b> A parallel example: עד יעבור עמך ה׳ — עד יעבור עם זו קנית; נשאו נהרות ה׳ — נשאו נהרות קולם, and many more. The meaning is: <b>the two ends of these cords you shall place upon the two settings</b> mentioned above, in the section of the ephod before the section of the choshen." "<b>And you shall place</b> these two settings <b>upon</b> the ends <b>of the shoulder-pieces of the ephod</b> — the doubled ones that descend from its two neck-parts slightly, <b>toward its front</b>, meaning toward its upper edge on the ephod that comes from behind and folds slightly to the front of the High Priest by means of the band with which he is girded. Above, the making of the settings was written; here, their attachment is written."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The parallel examples are cases where a possessive suffix on a noun refers to an implicit appositional phrase involving the divine name; the Hebrew citations are rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:57.341537225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}